infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Fake vs mock: two doubles, opposite purposes
  desc A fake checks state and survives refactors; a mock checks interactions and breaks on call shape
  compares
    - label Fake / stub
      children
        - label Provides realistic state
          desc In-memory Map you save to and read back
        - label You assert the outcome
          desc The order is persisted, the total is right
        - label Breaks only on behavior change
          desc Survives any behavior-preserving refactor
        - label Use for code you own
          desc Domain services, your own repositories
    - label Mock
      children
        - label Records call expectations
          desc Programmed with expectations about calls
        - label You assert the interaction
          desc charge(amount) called once with this arg
        - label Breaks on any call-shape change
          desc Split one save into two and it goes red
        - label Use at boundaries you do not control
          desc Payment, email, clock, third-party HTTP
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
